      "created_at": "2016-02-13T18:44:56.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My friend and I were playing a game of Villains with La Capitan, and on our first turn we used Adamant Writhe to throw Chiquito to the bottom of her deck. &nbsp;Did we do this right? &nbsp;Is La Capitan supposed to be ridiculously easy if you can permanently get rid of her little monkey?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It was kind of an odd game all around. &nbsp;MVP was Plague Rat - the heroes did very little damage to the villains. &nbsp;Mostly, Plague Rat did the damage, and Writhe didn't die. &nbsp;Maze of Mirrors from the evil carnival meant whenever Writhe tried to deal damage, it would get redirected to him, and then redirected away from him at -2.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:37.433Z",
